sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-07--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2025-wisdom-07: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.47";
    dc:description "Classic regulative experiments are published measurements of recovery after displacement, so the open-loop versus feedback contrast can be examined for particular organs. Those records are not a harmonized dataset, and they do not encode the molecular steps or show that the stored target is a complex data structure. The feedback idea is partly testable; the data-structure clause is not resolved by what is public.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: After a defined anatomical perturbation, test whether the system reduces an error relative to a species-typical target by alternative molecular routes, or instead follows a fixed sequence that does not depend on the remaining error. Return toward the target by more than one route favors closed-loop homeostasis; a single obligatory sequence favors open-loop development.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Error relative to a target can be redescribed as late-acting induction without a stored setpoint.", "Nothing currently measures whether a setpoint is a complex data structure rather than a scalar or a gradient.", "Perturbation-recovery series are scattered through the embryological literature and are not one dataset.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.64"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.473"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-07--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2025-wisdom-07 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.4"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-07--grok>.
